### 1. The Villain

Teams with deep distributed-systems experience assume AI systems are just another infrastructure problem, and apply the patterns they know — horizontal scaling, standard error-handling, stateless APIs — only to discover that AI systems break those rules at every layer: outputs don't fail predictably, GPUs cannot be over-subscribed like VMs, networking requirements inside the data center are a category jump, and the economics of context windows make "stateless" architecture silently expensive.

The misconception is not ignorance of AI. It is competence in traditional systems creating a false sense of readiness.

